"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 1\n"
"wt.ch01.title = Getting started\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch01_s01.title = Visit the Online Center\n"
"wt.ch01_s01.goal = Junior is in Kusanagi City, the real world, with his friends. Head for the Online Center to sign up for the game.\n"
"wt.ch01_s01.help = The Online Center is close to the street corner where the story begins. Go inside and talk to the Account Clerk. That scene finishes the sign-up and moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch01_s02.title = Log in, first partner\n"
"wt.ch01_s02.goal = You are signed up. Enter the game world and report to the Login Room in Asuka City.\n"
"wt.ch01_s02.help = After the Online Center, the Chamber Room takes Junior into the game. In the Login Room of Asuka City, talk to the Account Clerk to finish logging in.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch01_s03.goal = Go to the Main Lobby in Asuka City and find the Tamer Service. It hands out your first partner.\n"
"wt.ch01_s03.help = The Tamer Service offers three starter packs, called A, B and C, and downloads the one you choose. Pick any: the story goes on the same way with each of them.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch01_s04.title = Meet Tamer Genji\n"
"wt.ch01_s04.goal = A tamer named Genji waits in the Central Sector of Asuka City. Find him in the streets near the bridge.\n"
"wt.ch01_s04.help = Speak to Genji where the Central Sector meets the bridge. After you talk, a battle starts.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch01_s05.goal = Genji's battle is over, but your business with him is not. The talk goes on in the same street.\n"
"wt.ch01_s05.help = The follow-up scene plays when the Central Sector loads again after the battle. If nothing happens, step out of the street and come back in. This moves the story on to the next step.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch01_s06.title = Travel to Seiryu City\n"
"wt.ch01_s06.goal = Asuka City is open now. Cross the Asuka Bridge, go through Central Park and the Wire Forest, then past Divermon's Lake to Wind Prairie. Seiryu City is off Wind Prairie; the East Station is further on, past Kicking Forest.\n"
"wt.ch01_s06.help = The Seiryu Leader tests you in a battle, then gives you a Silver ID and the Seiryu Badge. The scene in Seiryu City sends you on to the East Station.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch01_x01.title = New faces around Asuka\n"
"wt.ch01_x01.goal = Optional. From this step on, several buildings in Asuka City have new people inside.\n"
"wt.ch01_x01.help = Look into the Digimon Lab, the Inn (both floors), the Junk Shop, Lamb Chop and El Dorado.\n"
"\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 2\n"
"wt.ch02.title = The southern road\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s01.title = East Station\n"
"wt.ch02_s01.goal = Seiryu City is behind you. Go back to Wind Prairie, then on through Kicking Forest to the East Station in the East Sector; a scene plays there.\n"
"wt.ch02_s01.help = The scene at the East Station is the whole step. When it ends, the story moves on and sends you to the South Station.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s02.title = South Sector, Zanbamon\n"
"wt.ch02_s02.goal = Next stop is the South Station in the South Sector. A short scene plays when you arrive.\n"
"wt.ch02_s02.help = The scene is the whole step. It moves the story on to the Jungle Grave.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s03.goal = Go to the Jungle Grave in the South Sector and speak to Zanbamon. A battle follows.\n"
"wt.ch02_s03.help = The talk with Zanbamon leads into a battle. After you win, a second scene with Zanbamon plays and moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s04.goal = Look for the Swamp Inn and the Shaman House in the South Sector. Voice and Sepikmon are at the Shaman House.\n"
"wt.ch02_s04.help = Talk to the person at the Swamp Inn first. Only after that does the scene with Voice and Sepikmon play at the Shaman House.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s05.title = Messages and the Lake\n"
"wt.ch02_s05.goal = Several people in the East Sector and in Asuka City have to be spoken to in turn. Start at the Protocol Ruins in the East Sector.\n"
"wt.ch02_s05.help = The order is: the Protocol Ruins, then the Asuka Bridge, then the streets by the Cargo Tower in the Central Sector. Each person talks to you only after the one before. The last talk lets the scene at Divermon's Lake start.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s06.goal = Go to Divermon's Lake in the East Sector. A scene with Man and Nick waits there.\n"
"wt.ch02_s06.help = Talk to the person who now stands by the lake to start the scene with Man and Nick. It moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s07.title = Central Sector, Sewers\n"
"wt.ch02_s07.goal = Back in Asuka City, speak to the person in the streets of the Central Sector by the Cargo Tower.\n"
"wt.ch02_s07.help = This person only appears now. The talk is needed before the Asuka Sewers give you what you need.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s08.goal = Someone in the Asuka Sewers has an item for you. Go and get it.\n"
"wt.ch02_s08.help = Once the Central Sector talk is done, talk to the character in the Asuka Sewers who gives you the item. You need it for the Shaman House.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s09.title = Shaman House again\n"
"wt.ch02_s09.goal = With the item, go back to the Shaman House in the South Sector and speak to Sepikmon.\n"
"wt.ch02_s09.help = The scene with Sepikmon gives you the Smelly Herb and moves the story on. It only starts once you hold the item from the Sewers.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch02_s10.title = The Suzaku Leader\n"
"wt.ch02_s10.goal = Go to Suzaku Hall in Suzaku City and speak to the Suzaku Leader. A battle follows.\n"
"wt.ch02_s10.help = The talk leads into a battle with the Suzaku Leader. Win it to get the Suzaku Badge; a second scene then moves the story on.\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 3\n"
"wt.ch03.title = Asuka City again\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch03_s01.title = Kail in Asuka City\n"
"wt.ch03_s01.goal = Return to the Main Lobby in Asuka City. Kail and many other people are there.\n"
"wt.ch03_s01.help = A long group scene plays, and a scene with Kail follows it. Together they move the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch03_s02.goal = Kail waits for you in the Underground Path in Asuka City.\n"
"wt.ch03_s02.help = The Underground Path is reached from the streets of the Central Sector. The scene with Kail moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch03_s03.goal = Go to the Master Room in Asuka City. Kail, the Game Master and the DO Guard are there.\n"
"wt.ch03_s03.help = Play this scene first. The scene with Kail in the Main Lobby only moves the story on once this one has been seen.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch03_s04.goal = Go back to the Main Lobby in Asuka City and speak to Kail.\n"
"wt.ch03_s04.help = The scene with Kail moves the story on. It needs the Master Room scene to have happened first.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch03_s05.title = Qing Long Chief\n"
"wt.ch03_s05.goal = Go to the Reliability Spot in the South Sector, where the Qing Long Chief welcomes you.\n"
"wt.ch03_s05.help = The scene there is the whole step. You get the DE Sincerity, and the story moves on.\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 4\n"
"wt.ch04.title = Byakko City\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch04_s01.title = Cave to HiAndromon\n"
"wt.ch04_s01.goal = You have the DE Sincerity, a Digi-Egg. The person in the Bios Swamp, in the South Sector, answers differently once you carry it. Then go to the Underground Cave in Byakko City, in the West Sector.\n"
"wt.ch04_s01.help = The Bios Swamp person has a different line for you only while the DE Sincerity is in your pack. The scene in the Underground Cave is the whole step; it sends you on to the Byakko Leader.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch04_s02.goal = Go to the Mirage Room in the West Sector and speak to the Byakko Leader. A battle follows.\n"
"wt.ch04_s02.help = The talk leads into a battle. Win it to get the Byakko Badge; a second scene then moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch04_s03.goal = Go to the Operation Room in the West Sector and speak to HiAndromon. A battle follows.\n"
"wt.ch04_s03.help = Win the battle with HiAndromon to get the Rusty Rifle. The story moves on afterwards.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch04_x01.title = The Seabed\n"
"wt.ch04_x01.goal = Optional. From this chapter on, the UG Lake in the South Sector has a way down into the Seabed, a web of underground tunnels.\n"
"wt.ch04_x01.help = The tunnels run under the Sewers, Duel Island, Kicking Forest and the UG Lake; under the bridges; under Divermon's Lake and the South and West Sectors; under Shell Beach, Plug Cape, South Cape and the Lake of Ice; and under Central Park, Bulk Bridge and Phoenix Bay. A junction tunnel links most of them. One dead end holds two chests.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch04_x02.title = The Seabed forge\n"
"wt.ch04_x02.goal = Optional. A weapon forge is hidden in the Seabed. It upgrades weapons for those who bring the right parts.\n"
"wt.ch04_x02.help = The forge is in a tunnel that only the other Seabed tunnels reach, where Seehomon and Depthmon work. Speak to a smith once, then again with the right usable item in your pack: you get a stronger weapon, and the item (and the weapon one grade below, if you carry it) is taken. Two upgrades are offered.\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 5\n"
"wt.ch05.title = West Sector rebels\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch05_s01.title = Sewers, Secret Room\n"
"wt.ch05_s01.goal = Go to the Sewers in the West Sector. WaruMonzaemon and Lisa are there, and a battle follows.\n"
"wt.ch05_s01.help = The first scene leads into a battle. After you win, a short scene with Lisa, Numemon and Lucky Mouse moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch05_s02.goal = The Secret Room is a hideout off the Sewers in the West Sector. Go there; a battle takes place.\n"
"wt.ch05_s02.help = A scene with Lucky Mouse, Lisa, Kail, General and Attacker leads into a battle. Afterwards a scene with Attacker, Lisa, Kail and Kurt moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch05_s03.goal = Go to the Secret Room again. The scene there points you to the Suzaku UG Lake in the South Sector.\n"
"wt.ch05_s03.help = After the scene with Kail, Kurt and Lisa in the Secret Room, a scene is waiting at the Suzaku UG Lake. Visit the lake, then return to the Secret Room.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch05_s04.goal = Go back to the Secret Room in the West Sector.\n"
"wt.ch05_s04.help = Lisa, Keith, Nick and Kail are there. The scene moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch05_s05.title = Datamon and Teddy\n"
"wt.ch05_s05.goal = Go to the Control Room in Asuka City and speak to Datamon. A battle takes place.\n"
"wt.ch05_s05.help = Datamon fights you; afterwards he gives you the Rusty Glove. Another scene with Datamon moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch05_s06.goal = Go to the Master Room in Asuka City. Two scenes play there.\n"
"wt.ch05_s06.help = The two scenes play one after the other. The second one moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch05_s07.goal = Go to the A.o.A Headquarters in Asuka City. Guards stand in the way, and two battles follow.\n"
"wt.ch05_s07.help = Guard A, Guard B and Guard C come first, then the Game Master. When both battles are won, the story can go on in the Main Lobby.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch05_s08.goal = Return to the Main Lobby in Asuka City and speak to Teddy.\n"
"wt.ch05_s08.help = The scene with Teddy moves the story on.\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 6\n"
"wt.ch06.title = Byakko and Suzaku\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch06_s01.title = See the General\n"
"wt.ch06_s01.goal = Go back to the Underground Cave in Byakko City. The General is waiting there.\n"
"wt.ch06_s01.help = The scene with the General is the whole step. It moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch06_s02.title = Talk with Patamon\n"
"wt.ch06_s02.goal = Go to Suzaku Hall in Suzaku City and meet Patamon.\n"
"wt.ch06_s02.help = The scene with Patamon is the whole step. It moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch06_s03.title = Bug Maze Pit\n"
"wt.ch06_s03.goal = Go to the Bug Maze Pit in the Network Break. A battle takes place there.\n"
"wt.ch06_s03.help = A battle starts in the pit. After you win, a last scene plays and the story moves on to the Amaterasu server.\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 7\n"
"wt.ch07.title = Amaterasu server\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch07_s01.title = Qing Long Chief\n"
"wt.ch07_s01.goal = Go to Qing Long City in the East Sector, now on the Amaterasu server. The Qing Long Chief is there, and a battle follows.\n"
"wt.ch07_s01.help = Win the battle to get the Blue ID Pass. A last scene then moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch07_s02.title = Zhu Que Hall, UG Lake\n"
"wt.ch07_s02.goal = Go to Zhu Que Hall in Zhu Que City. A battle takes place there.\n"
"wt.ch07_s02.help = A scene leads into a battle. After you win, a last scene gives you the Red ID Pass and moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch07_s03.goal = Go to the Zhu Que UG Lake in the South Sector. A scene plays there.\n"
"wt.ch07_s03.help = The scene is the whole step. You get the DE Knowledge, and the story moves on.\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 8\n"
"wt.ch08.title = North Sector\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_s01.title = Genbu, Chamber Room\n"
"wt.ch08_s01.goal = Go to the Battle Gate in the North Sector and speak to the Genbu Leader. A battle follows.\n"
"wt.ch08_s01.help = Win the battle to get the Genbu Badge. A second scene then moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_s02.goal = Go to the Chamber Room in the North Sector and speak to the Chamber Officer.\n"
"wt.ch08_s02.help = The scene with the Chamber Officer moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_s03.goal = The Chamber Room has gates to other places. Use the one to the real world and go to Kusanagi City.\n"
"wt.ch08_s03.help = The trip to the real world is part of this step. A scene in Kusanagi City has to play before the Chamber Room scene can finish the step. The other gate leads to the Ice Dungeon.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_s04.goal = Return to the Chamber Room in the North Sector.\n"
"wt.ch08_s04.help = A last scene in the Chamber Room moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_s05.title = Master Room and Prison\n"
"wt.ch08_s05.goal = Go to the Master Room in Asuka City. Lisa, Teddy, Keith and Nick are there.\n"
"wt.ch08_s05.help = The first scene there sets the next errand: the Prison Tower.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_s06.goal = Go to the Prison Tower in Asuka City. Lisa, the Game Master and Teddy are involved.\n"
"wt.ch08_s06.help = The scenes in the Prison Tower have to play before the Master Room scene can move the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_s07.goal = Return to the Master Room in Asuka City.\n"
"wt.ch08_s07.help = The last scene there, with Lisa, Nick, Keith and Teddy, moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_x01.title = The Circuit Board\n"
"wt.ch08_x01.goal = Optional. From this chapter on, maps in several sectors have an entrance to the Circuit Board, a second web of underground tunnels.\n"
"wt.ch08_x01.help = The entrance tunnels lead on to deeper ones: a tunnel with Black Kingz and Numemon, the Black Kingz' den, and two last tunnels with guides to the exits of both servers. Duels and fights wait inside.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch08_x02.title = The Black Kingz' den\n"
"wt.ch08_x02.goal = Optional. The Black Kingz keep a den in the Circuit Board. Its members challenge you to card duels.\n"
"wt.ch08_x02.help = The den is reached from the deeper tunnels. Eight Black Kingz accept a card duel. A duel is offered until you win it; after that the winner only talks. Six of them hand over a card for the first win, and one more gives a key item.\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 9\n"
"wt.ch09.title = Two more ID passes\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch09_s01.title = White ID Pass\n"
"wt.ch09_s01.goal = Go to the Bai Hu Dome in Bai Hu City. A battle takes place there.\n"
"wt.ch09_s01.help = A scene leads into a battle. After you win, a last scene gives you the White ID Pass and moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch09_s02.title = Black ID Pass\n"
"wt.ch09_s02.goal = Go to the Battle Gate in the North Sector, on the Amaterasu server. A battle takes place there.\n"
"wt.ch09_s02.help = A scene leads into a battle. After you win, a last scene gives you the Black ID Pass and moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch09_s03.title = Amaterasu Bridge\n"
"wt.ch09_s03.goal = Go to the Amaterasu Bridge in the Central Sector. Lisa, Teddy and Nick are involved.\n"
"wt.ch09_s03.help = A scene with the Resistance plays first. A second scene with Teddy and Nick moves the story on.\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 10\n"
"wt.ch10.title = Spy Satellite\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch10_s01.title = A.o.A HQ, Login Room\n"
"wt.ch10_s01.goal = Go to the A.o.A Headquarters in Amaterasu City. Several scenes play there in turn.\n"
"wt.ch10_s01.help = The scenes include a battle with the Chief Officer. When the last of them has played, the next stop is the Login Room.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch10_s02.goal = Go to the Login Room in Amaterasu City. Teddy, Kail and Kurt are there.\n"
"wt.ch10_s02.help = The scene with Teddy, Kail and Kurt moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch10_s03.title = A.o.A HQ again\n"
"wt.ch10_s03.goal = Go to the A.o.A Headquarters in Asuka City.\n"
"wt.ch10_s03.help = A scene plays when you arrive. It moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch10_s04.title = A.o.A HQ once more\n"
"wt.ch10_s04.goal = Go to the A.o.A Headquarters in Amaterasu City.\n"
"wt.ch10_s04.help = Two scenes play there, one after the other. The second one moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch10_s05.title = Satellite to Snatchmon\n"
"wt.ch10_s05.goal = The Spy Satellite is reached from the A.o.A Headquarters in Amaterasu City. Go to its first floor, the Gunslinger 1F.\n"
"wt.ch10_s05.help = The blocks on this floor open from panels. A scene on the floor moves the story on.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch10_s06.goal = Go to the Control Room in the Spy Satellite. A battle with Lord Megadeath waits there.\n"
"wt.ch10_s06.help = A scene leads into the battle. When you win, the next scene in the same room starts the last fight of this part.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch10_s07.goal = Lord Megadeath is beaten. Snatchmon waits in the same Control Room.\n"
"wt.ch10_s07.help = The scene with Snatchmon leads straight into the last battle of the story. Get ready before it starts.\n"
"\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 11\n"
"wt.ch11.title = The last battle\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch11_s01.title = The final battle\n"
"wt.ch11_s01.goal = The scene with Snatchmon ends in the last battle of the story, in the Control Room of the Spy Satellite. It has three opponents. Win it and the ending plays.\n"
"wt.ch11_s01.help = Heal and stock up before the Snatchmon scene: the battle starts as soon as it ends. After the ending you are back in Kusanagi City, the real world, where a last scene plays. On the European disc that scene opens the extra chapter.\n"
"\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- chapter 12 (EU only)\n"
"wt.ch12.title = Extra chapter\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch12_s01.title = Login Room tour\n"
"wt.ch12_s01.goal = After the last scene in Kusanagi City, log in again from the Chamber Room. You arrive in the Login Room of Amaterasu City, where the Tour Leader is waiting.\n"
"wt.ch12_s01.help = The scene with the Tour Leader plays when you arrive, and only once.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch12_s02.title = Four challengers\n"
"wt.ch12_s02.goal = Four Digimon wait for a fight: one in Qing Long City, two at the Protocol Ruins and one in Tyranno Valley. All are in the East Sector. Beat all four.\n"
"wt.ch12_s02.help = They offer a fight only if you hold a certain set of five items, in your pack or equipped. Without the set there is no fight. You may take them on in any order. Once all four are beaten, the clerk at the Arena Front Desk reacts.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch12_s03.title = Kurt at the Arena\n"
"wt.ch12_s03.goal = The four are beaten. Go to the Arena Front Desk in Amaterasu City. Kurt waits in the Digimon Arena, and a battle follows.\n"
"wt.ch12_s03.help = Speak to the clerk at the desk. Kurt's scene plays when you enter the Digimon Arena, and the battle comes right after it. Winning it is the last step of the extra chapter that this walkthrough follows.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch12_x01.title = A set of five weapons\n"
"wt.ch12_x01.goal = Five weapons can be made in the North Sector.\n"
"wt.ch12_x01.help = Kulon Weapons in the North Sector has five smiths. Speak to a smith once, then again with the right usable item in your pack: you get one of the five weapons, and the item (and the weapon one grade below, if you carry it) is taken. These five are the set the four challengers ask for. Hold all five, in your pack or equipped.\n"
"\n"
"wt.ch12_x02.title = Partners to win back\n"
"wt.ch12_x02.goal = Optional. Partners you have not recruited yet can still join you in the Circuit Board tunnels of this chapter.\n"
"wt.ch12_x02.help = Two deep Circuit Board tunnels hold a fighter for each of the eight partners. A fighter stands there only while its partner is not yet yours, and only once every partner you have is level 45 or more. Where it stands depends on the way you came in. Talk to it twice: a fight starts, and after you win the partner joins you and you get a key item.\n"
"\n"
"# ---------------------------------------------------------------- areas\n"
"wt.area_kusanagi.title = Kusanagi City\n"
"wt.area_kusanagi.help = Kusanagi City is the real world, where the story starts. Only two places matter here: the street corner and the Online Center. The story comes back here once more, later, through a Chamber Room gate.\n"
"\n"
"wt.area_asuka.title = Asuka City\n"
"wt.area_asuka.help = Asuka City is the first town and the story keeps coming back to it. At the start: the Login Room, the Main Lobby (starter partner), then the Central Sector, where Genji waits. Later scenes use the Underground Path, the Asuka Sewers, the Master Room, the Control Room, the Prison Tower and A.o.A Headquarters.\n"
"\n"
"wt.area_east.title = East Sector\n"
"wt.area_east.help = The East Sector holds Seiryu City, the East Station, the Protocol Ruins and Divermon's Lake. On the Amaterasu server it also holds Qing Long City, where the Qing Long Chief fights you. The European extra chapter sends you to Qing Long City, the Protocol Ruins and Tyranno Valley.\n"
"\n"
"wt.area_south.title = South Sector\n"
"wt.area_south.help = The South Sector holds the South Station, the Jungle Grave, the Swamp Inn, the Shaman House and the Reliability Spot, where the Qing Long Chief welcomes you. The Suzaku UG Lake and, on the Amaterasu server, the Zhu Que UG Lake are here too.\n"
"\n"
"wt.area_suzaku.title = Suzaku and Zhu Que\n"
"wt.area_suzaku.help = Suzaku City, called Zhu Que City on the Amaterasu server, has Suzaku Hall (Zhu Que Hall there). On the first server the Suzaku Leader waits there and Patamon turns up later. On the Amaterasu server Zhu Que Hall is the setting of a battle that gives the Red ID Pass.\n"
"\n"
"wt.area_west.title = West Sector\n"
"wt.area_west.help = Byakko City and the West Sector come in this order: the Underground Cave, the Mirage Room (Byakko Leader), the Operation Room (HiAndromon), then the Sewers and the Secret Room, the rebels' hideout off the Sewers. The Underground Cave is visited again later.\n"
"\n"
"wt.area_north.title = North Sector\n"
"wt.area_north.help = The North Sector has the Battle Gate, where the Genbu Leader waits, and the Chamber Room, whose gates lead to the real world and the Ice Dungeon. The Amaterasu server has its own Battle Gate, where the Black ID Pass is won.\n"
"\n"
"wt.area_amaterasu.title = Amaterasu server\n"
"wt.area_amaterasu.help = The Amaterasu server repeats many places of the first server. Here the walkthrough uses the Bai Hu Dome, the Amaterasu Bridge, the Login Room and the A.o.A Headquarters of Amaterasu City. Other Amaterasu places are listed under their own sector. On the European disc the extra chapter starts in the Login Room here and ends at the Digimon Arena.\n"
"\n"
"wt.area_network.title = Network Break\n"
"wt.area_network.help = The Network Break has the Bug Maze Pit. The Spy Satellite is reached from the A.o.A Headquarters in Amaterasu City: first the Gunslinger 1F, whose blocks open from panels, then the Control Room, where Lord Megadeath and Snatchmon wait. The last battle follows Snatchmon.\n";
